Translation patch: `bytes::BufMut` methods used on `Vec<u8>`

Change: A crate-local trait `io::BufMut` with exactly the `put_*` methods the crate uses, implemented for `Vec<u8>` with the bodies `bytes` 1.12 gives them (`put_slice` = `extend_from_slice`; `put_u8` etc. = `put_slice` of the little-endian bytes; `put_uint_le`/`put_int_le` = `put_slice(&n.to_le_bytes()[..nbytes])`; `put_f32_le`/`put_f64_le` = `put_u32_le(n.to_bits())`/`put_u64_le(n.to_bits())`). `BufMutExt` and the in-scope files (io, misc/raw/*, value) import it instead of `bytes::BufMut`.
Why: `bytes::BufMut for Vec<u8>` is an external, `unsafe` implementation (`chunk_mut`/`advance_mut`), and its provided methods are foreign bodies Charon does not translate.
Behaviour: Identical for `Vec<u8>`: each body is copied from `bytes` 1.12.1 `buf_mut.rs` (the `Vec<u8>` impl overrides only `put_slice`). The only difference is the panic message when `nbytes > 8` (both panic). Every user of `BufMutExt` in the crate uses it on `Vec<u8>` (the crate compiles with all features).

